FINAL ANSWER:
Pulling surviving-line counts with `git blame` rather than commit counts. The results are in.

**Who wrote the live code in `src/Parser`**

Graham Campbell is the main author. I counted three of their addresses as one person. That is a guess from the matching name and address pattern, and nothing was written to `.mailmap`. Scope: HEAD, 1,006 non-blank lines (1,187 with blank lines), 9 files, blame with `-w -M -C`.

| Author | Lines | Share | Commits (share) | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Graham Campbell (3 addresses, merged) | 673 | 66.9% | 33 (82.5%) | 2026-08-26 |
| Aiko Tanaka | 171 | 17.0% | 3 (7.5%) | 2026-08-26 |
| root `<root@localhost>` | 96 | 9.5% | 1 (2.5%) | 2026-08-26 |
| Your Name `<<email redacted>>` | 56 | 5.6% | 1 (2.5%) | 2026-08-26 |
| Vance Lucas | 8 | 0.8% | 0 | 2015-10-28 |
| Jonas Staudenmeir | 1 | 0.1% | 1 (2.5%) | 2024-07-20 |
| JT Smith | 1 | 0.1% | 1 (2.5%) | 2022-10-15 |

- **Merge detail:** Unmerged, Graham's lines are 333 under `<email redacted>`, 338 under the `<email redacted>` address, and 2 under `<email redacted>`.
- **Unattributable lines:** `root` and `Your Name` hold 152 lines (15.1%) under placeholder identities. Those lines can't be attributed to a person, and neither identity is someone to ask.
- **Bus factor:** 1 for `src/Parser`, because Graham alone holds 66.9% of the lines. Reaching 80% takes 2 authors. This counts surviving lines to a 50% threshold. It is not a measure of who understands the code.
- **Excluded:** `src/Parser/Unicode/CharTable.php` (431 lines, generated) is left out of every number. StyleCI Bot (1 line, 1 commit) is excluded and gets no credit.
- **Mechanical rewrites:** I checked 48 commits. None were set aside, and no reformat commit was ignored.
- **Copy detection:** Detection moved 72 lines in 3 files to other authors. With it, Graham has 673 lines (66.9%) and Vance Lucas has 8 lines. Without it, Graham has 681 lines (67.7%) and Vance Lucas has none.

**Who to ask about `Lexer.php`**

Ask Graham Campbell. They hold 48 of 48 lines (100%) in `Lexer.php`, and `Lexer.php` is not sampled. Unmerged:

- `<email redacted>` holds 44 lines (91.7%). Its last commit was 2020-06-07, so that address is inactive.
- The noreply address holds 4 lines (8.3%), last commit 2026-08-24.
- `<email redacted>` holds 0 lines.

The strong merge says this is one active person.

31.3% of the lines in `Lexer.php` (15 of 48) were moved or copied in from `src/Loader/Lines.php`, `src/Lines.php` and `src/Loader/Value.php`. Blame credits those lines to whoever wrote them originally. I did not trace who that was for each line.

**Who to ask about escape handling**

Ask Aiko Tanaka. `Escape.php` is the only file in `src/Parser` named for escaping. They hold 171 of 171 lines (100%) across 2 commits, with the last commit on 2026-08-26 (active). `EntryParser.php` also mentions "escape", but I did not run blame on it separately. Its authorship is covered only by the directory table above.

**For the audit**

- Aiko Tanaka's escape code is concentrated in one person's hands and is recent.
- Graham's `Lexer.php` lines are mostly from 2020, and the merge was only run in memory.
- These numbers show whose code is still there, not its quality or who reviewed it.
